Open a room on a host with no container runtime (a Cowork cloud sandbox):
every door's guest side is where its broker listens, sockets live in a
private run dir (world-writable dirs refused), an injecting parent
(HTTPS_PROXY) is refused unless GUEST_ROOM_ALLOW_INJECTING_PARENT=1 and is
then named in the rulebook, and the rulebook says NO WALLS in as many words.

profiles/allowlist-door.ts is the egress door's decision without its
chokepoint: `connect {host}` answered from `host=` caveats via checkCaveats
over a real unix socket, fail closed; a door with no allowlist refuses to
serve. Proven by features/nopodman.feature + nopodman.test.ts, which run
without podman. Engine files are untouched (the names-no-guest test holds).

Refs: burndown gr-cowork-port (off-board; no tracking issue)

