+# Executed against guest-room/profiles/nopodman.ts by guest-room.test.ts.
+# Some hosts have no container runtime: the guest shares a filesystem and a uid
+# with its brokers. The nopodman profile opens a room THERE — every door's guest
+# side is where its broker actually listens — and renders a rulebook that says
+# so: doors, no walls. The rulebook is a default a careful guest honors, not a
+# fence, and it names the one thing that can still act as the operator past any
+# door: a credential-injecting parent gateway.
+#
+# What this feature does NOT claim: confinement. Nothing here stops a process
+# from reaching past a door; see docs/working-in-a-cowork-sandbox.md (gap list).
+
+Feature: A room can be opened without walls, and its rulebook says so
+
+  Scenario: same-host doors — the guest connects where the broker listens
+    Given the hotel's door catalog and rooms
+    When the room "dev" is opened without walls
+    Then the open doors are "keeper, net, scout"
+    And every door's in-room socket is where its broker listens
+    And the rulebook says there are no walls
+
+  Scenario: what is not granted is still denied by name
+    Given the hotel's door catalog and rooms
+    When the room "read" is opened without walls
+    Then the rulebook grants mention "scout"
+    And the rulebook denies "keeper"
+    And the rulebook denies "net"
+
+  Scenario: an injecting parent is refused unless the room says otherwise
+    Given the hotel's door catalog and rooms
+    And an injecting gateway fronts the host
+    When the room "read" is opened without walls
+    Then opening is refused
+    When the room says an injecting parent is acceptable
+    And the room "read" is opened without walls
+    Then the open doors are "scout"
+    And the rulebook names the injecting gateway
